WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.563
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.563 --> 00:00:10.435
I had just finished the first year
of work at an investment firm,

00:00:10.435 --> 00:00:14.690
and received my first performance review,
it was bad.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:20.254
Note, I am humbly telling you it was bad
[INAUDIBLE] my reviewer actually admitted,

00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:23.035
you get to inflate my
scores a little bit so

00:00:23.035 --> 00:00:26.316
it didn't look so horrible,
that level of bad.

00:00:26.316 --> 00:00:29.288
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; My immediate reaction,

00:00:29.288 --> 00:00:32.150
I am too stupid to make it in investing.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:36.870
My next reaction,
I have to punish myself for my failure.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:42.794
I left the office and began sprinting
through a still chilly Boston night,

00:00:42.794 --> 00:00:43.800
I hate running.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.775
I don't ever run for exercise.

00:00:46.775 --> 00:00:50.390
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; But every time I felt I need to punish

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:56.130
myself, I would sprint and
then my lungs began to burn.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:01:01.830
I had failed and the voice in my
head said, you should suffer for it.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:08.100
If a friend came to me, upset with a bad
performance review or a terrible fight.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.030
I wouldn't tell her to go run
some laps as a punishment.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:16.760
I would hug her and help her figure
out a way out of this difficult time.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:24.150
So why would I treat myself differently
than I would to a close friend?

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:28.330
Think of the voice you use
to criticize yourself.

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:33.900
That interview was so horrible, why
couldn't I come up with better answers?

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:38.315
Or I said the dumbest thing on the date,
I'm single forever.

00:01:38.315 --> 00:01:41.550
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; We've

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:44.490
internalized this negative
self-talk as normal.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:49.860
We aren't even aware of it and
we don't question it.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.910
This voice gives us feedback
on our performance.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:58.360
We believe it makes us be better,
try harder, reach higher.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.712
It's our internal coach but

00:02:00.712 --> 00:02:06.200
it's feedback from a coach who
doesn't really know how to coach.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:11.014
Research shows that athletes are more
motivated by positive coaches

00:02:11.014 --> 00:02:12.430
than hostile ones.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:19.970
Yet, when it comes to coaching ourselves,
we tend to be more hostile than positive.

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:24.959
I thought I was becoming
tougher by punishing myself for

00:02:24.959 --> 00:02:28.470
my failures but the opposite was true.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:33.871
If wanted to be a great coach to
myself and improve my performance,

00:02:33.871 --> 00:02:39.369
I needed to train that voice in my
head to shush negative self talk and

00:02:39.369 --> 00:02:42.270
embrace self compassion instead.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:49.850
Self compassion is switch from
self judgment, to self kindness.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:54.379
It's filling the court to
assess you are so weak, and

00:02:54.379 --> 00:02:58.845
hiring the one who says,
I understand it's tough.

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:03.360
When your team is getting
blown out at half time,

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.865
you don't win the game by screaming,
you suck.

00:03:05.865 --> 00:03:10.072
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Coach K,

00:03:10.072 --> 00:03:13.174
the legendary Duke basketball coach,

00:03:13.174 --> 00:03:18.156
with the most wins in Division
one men's basketball history,

00:03:18.156 --> 00:03:23.890
says that his most reliable pep talk
to his players is, I believe in you.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:29.090
The positive impact of self
compassion is written in biology.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:33.425
When we are hard on ourselves,
our body doesn't realize that it's our

00:03:33.425 --> 00:03:39.390
self-talk and not someone else yelling
at us and releases stress hormones.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:43.873
When you sue on that problem or
beat yourself up over that failure,

00:03:43.873 --> 00:03:49.333
your body continues to release cortisol
diverting energy from the task at hand.

00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:54.932
That's why if you're a basketball player
and you miss the first free throw,

00:03:54.932 --> 00:04:00.632
you don't improve your chances of making
the next one by beating yourself up.

00:04:00.632 --> 00:04:04.128
You do it by taking a deep breath and
concentrating.

00:04:04.128 --> 00:04:09.965
As one of the greatest poets of
our generation Taylor Swift,

00:04:09.965 --> 00:04:13.977
tells us you need to
dress to shake it off.

00:04:13.977 --> 00:04:16.551
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Last week,

00:04:16.551 --> 00:04:22.173
I caught myself thinking I am not
strong enough to give this talk.

00:04:22.173 --> 00:04:24.897
I have too much going on.

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.622
It's going to be so bad.

00:04:26.622 --> 00:04:32.120
I am a disappointment but that's a lie.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.080
I am strong enough but
it's not about strength.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:41.290
I was drunk on cortisol and
I need to get my head back in the game.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:42.160
So how did I do it?

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:48.700
Four year ago, I wouldn't have I
would have kept beating myself up

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:55.577
all the way to a very mediocre draft,
in a terrible self-fulfilling prophecy.

00:04:55.577 --> 00:04:58.430
Today, when I realize
I'm beating myself up,

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:04.830
I bring up my inner Coach K,
who says, I believe in you and

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:09.847
I go through five steps
of self-compassion.

00:05:09.847 --> 00:05:12.310
First, name it.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:15.620
Name what it is they are actually feeling.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.020
I wasn't just stressed I was hurting.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:23.320
Because with everything else
going on in my life I didn't feel

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:28.200
I had capacity to do justice to
a topic that matters so much to me.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:32.896
I need to first understand
exactly what's wrong.

00:05:32.896 --> 00:05:37.610
Step two, feel it,

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:41.150
allow yourself to fully
embrace that feeling.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.880
Whether it's upset or
anger or disappointment.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:47.810
I was hurting and I wanted to cry.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:51.640
So I did, I didn't go for a sprint.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:53.960
I took a walk and I cried.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:57.800
A few years ago,
I would have felt crazy doing that.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.770
It was actually a natural human reaction.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:05.900
If my three year old niece Lena throwing
a tantrum, then suddenly stopping and

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:06.695
going back to play.

00:06:06.695 --> 00:06:10.820
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; The secret here is once you allow

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:16.720
yourself to deeply feel that feeling,
that negative emotion passes faster.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:22.050
Step three is my favorite,
comfort yourself.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:29.290
Ask yourself what would you say and
do if it was a friend and not yourself.

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:31.730
What do I need right now to feel better.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:35.440
I came back hum from my walk.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:39.180
I played the Drake as loud
as my speakers would allow.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.145
I danced and I eat chocolate.

00:06:41.145 --> 00:06:45.520
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; This step is not about problem solving,

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:48.410
it's about giving yourself
what you need there and then.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:53.490
Step four, hit a mental reset.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:59.930
Tell yourself that it sucks,
but it's okay and it will pass.

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:02.190
Now that you've felt your feelings,

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.810
you can have mental space
again to be rational.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:08.970
I've hanged out with a friend who gave
me drake and chocolate, he is cool.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:14.200
Now it's time for
a friend who helped me solve the problem.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.830
What do I need to get done and
how can I make it more manageable.

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:22.740
The fifth and last step is simply go.

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:27.770
If you're head back in the game,
it's time to take action.

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:30.320
What are your next steps?

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:34.367
I said down, I made it to the list,
and I wrote,

00:07:34.367 --> 00:07:39.836
remembering why I wanted to give
the speech in the first place and

00:07:39.836 --> 00:07:44.480
you might ask,
why didn't I just suck it up?

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:46.750
I should have sat down and
written the damn thing.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.760
I could have, but
my inner coach is smarter than that.

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:55.208
And she knows that if she
forces me to do something,

00:07:55.208 --> 00:08:01.630
the result won't be half as good as
when I'm ready to do it, want to do it.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:08.250
Self compassion allowed me to
free myself and be ready sooner.

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:14.500
Whether it's a bad interview or
a bad breakup, or

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:19.540
simply a bad day,
you want to pick yourself up faster, so

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.330
you're ready for
whatever life throws at you next.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:28.761
Coach Kay lives by next play philosophy,
whatever you've just done

00:08:28.761 --> 00:08:33.600
is not nearly as important as what
you're going to do right now.

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:38.099
As he says,
anyone who's had success or wants it,

00:08:38.099 --> 00:08:42.690
can't have a rearview mirror in their car.

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:45.660
They can't look back
they've got to look ahead.

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:51.380
Don't look back be a good
coach to yourself.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:55.442
Show yourself some self compassion,
name it,

00:08:55.442 --> 00:08:59.106
feel it, comfort yourself, reset, go.

00:08:59.106 --> 00:09:03.024
Five steps, you've got this.

00:09:03.024 --> 00:09:05.941
I believe in you.

00:09:05.941 --> 00:09:08.120
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:10.641
[MUSIC]

